<x-layouts.site title="For veterinarians, farriers and trainers" description="How equine professionals contribute attributed records to Horsefax, with the owner's authorization.">
    <x-page-header eyebrow="For professionals" title="Your work, credited and kept with the horse." lede="Veterinarians, farriers, trainers and breeders add what they know, with the owner's permission and their name attached." />
    <div class="wrap py-16 prose-hf max-w-[44em]">
        <h2 class="!mt-0">How contributions work</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Attributed:</strong> each entry shows who contributed it and in what role.</li>
            <li><strong>Authorized:</strong> professionals contribute to a horse's record by the owner's invitation.</li>
            <li><strong>Protected:</strong> owners decide who sees an entry, but cannot silently rewrite what a professional recorded. Disagreements go through the correction process, and the history is kept.</li>
            <li><strong>Labeled honestly:</strong> observations about temperament or suitability appear as your dated opinion, never as a Horsefax guarantee.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Available now, and next</h2>
        <p>Owners can already record your visits and attach your documents to the horse's record, labeled as owner-entered. Professional accounts, with invitations from owners and entries submitted in your own name, are the next step in our build.</p>
        <p>If you would like to be one of the first professional contributors, <a href="{{ route('contact') }}">tell us about your practice</a>.</p>
    </div>
</x-layouts.site>
